# 1 From a trace to a circle

The canonical partition function is Z(T)=Tr e^{−βH}. Inserting complete sets of field eigenstates at N Euclidean time slices, exactly as Lesson 79 sliced e^{−iHT} but with t→−iτ and T_Minkowski→β, produces

$$ Z(T) = ∫_{periodic} Dφ  exp( − S_E[φ] )

with τ running from 0 to β and the two ends identified because a trace identifies the last complete set with the first.

