# Summary

1. Tr e^{−H/T} is a Euclidean path integral of period 1/T.

2. Photons are periodic in τ; electrons are antiperiodic.

3. k⁰ becomes iω_n and ∫dk⁰/2π becomes T Σ_n.

4. T→0 is ordinary QED.

5. Thermal infrared physics is more severe; it is not computed here.

